      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name} I'm the kind of person who checks the 'inverted' box in any game with a controller. When I play VRC on handheld or android with controller, I don't wish to have only one axis inverted, that's just preference and my assumption was that it may be trivial to impliment. Apologies, but not understanding why a particular axis inversion not being accessible for standard use would require non-standard hardware. On PC, despite wishing it was just available in the settings where the other axis is already available, on android I don't have the luxury of inverting within steaminput. Perhaps that's an applicable use case if that's what you were inquiring for?",
